SUMMARY:Riley Clemmons at The Trust Performing Arts Center
DESCRIPTION:Nashville native Riley Clemmons is an accomplished composer\, performer\, producer and recording artist who has made her mark on the contemporary Christian music scene. Her breakout single “Broken Prayers” came in 2017\, followed by her self-titled album debut\, which quickly entered the Billboard Heatseekers chart.\n\nClemmons’ single “Fighting For Me” earned RIAA Gold Certification\, adding to recognition from Rolling Stone and People Magazine along with Dove and K-LOVE award nominations. Clemmons has brought her music to some of the biggest stages and platforms around\, from the “TODAY” Show and “FOX & Friends” to a landmark debut at the Grand Ole Opry. Drawing from real life and a wide range of musical influences\, she crafts songs that are as emotionally honest as they are catchy\, resonating with listeners beyond any single genre. \n            \n        \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/riley-clemmons-at-the-trust-performing-arts-center/
LOCATION:Lancaster Bible College\, 901 Eden Road\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/203115_event_md_219.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="The Trust Performing Arts Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@lbc.edu
END:VEVENT
