SUMMARY:PDF@Zoetropolis Presents Everything Everywhere All At Once
DESCRIPTION:What if you could see every life you might have lived? Would you find yourself—or lose yourself among the possibilities? The Zoetropolis America 250 series continues its exploration of Reinvention & Transformation with Everything Everywhere All at Once.  \n\n\n\nMichelle Yeoh stars as Evelyn Wang\, a Chinese American immigrant juggling a struggling laundromat\, an IRS audit\, and a family she can’t quite hold together—until an encounter with the multiverse sends her hurtling through the lives she might have led. Wildly inventive\, funny\, and moving\, the film takes America’s promise of self-reinvention to an extraordinary extreme. If we could become anyone\, what would make this particular life worth choosing? And can kindness offer a meaningful response to a world that seems increasingly overwhelming? \n\n\n\n Join us for a brief pre-screening presentation\, the film\, and a post-screening discussion. A specialty cocktail inspired by the film will be available to complement the evening. No philosophy background required—just curiosity and a willingness to venture into the multiverse. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/pdfzoetropolis-presents-everything-everywhere-all-at-once/
LOCATION:Zoetropolis Cinema Stillhouse\, 112 North Water Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/EEAAOPOSTER2.webp
ORGANIZER;CN="Zoetropolis":MAILTO:info@zoetropolis.com
END:VEVENT
